    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-4-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the essence of NLP?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>categorizing human language into happy or sad</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. NLP is not only about happy or sad. Its essence is interpreting meaning or sentiment without a human doing it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>interpreting meaning or sentiment without having to have a human do it</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. NLP uses code to interpret meaning or sentiment in text, so a human does not have to read it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>finding outliers in sentiment and examining them</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Outliers are not the main point. The essence of NLP is interpreting meaning or sentiment without a human doing it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-4-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What are some things you might look for while cleaning data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>characters in other languages</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Characters in other languages can trip up algorithms, but empty spots, like rows with no reviews, are worth finding too.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>blank rows or columns</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Empty spots, like rows with no reviews, are worth finding. But characters in other languages can also trip up algorithms.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Characters in other languages can trip up algorithms, and rows with no reviews are worth finding too.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
